You own a property in Hauts-de-France and are torn between listing
            it on Airbnb or signing a traditional long-term lease? This is one
            of the most common questions we receive at Welqo. The answer depends
            on your profile, location and appetite for management. This guide
            gives you the tools to make an informed choice.

## Advantages of short-term rental (Airbnb)

A well-managed short-term rental in Hauts-de-France generates on
            average 40–80% more revenue than a traditional unfurnished long-term
            lease. In Lille, a 45 m² one-bedroom rented at €700/month long-term
            can earn €1,400–€1,800 gross per month on Airbnb. Flexibility, no
            payment risk, and better property upkeep are additional advantages.

## Advantages of long-term rental

One tenant, one lease, one monthly transfer. Long-term rental
            requires minimal day-to-day involvement, offers predictable income
            for loan repayments, lower operating costs, and fewer administrative
            constraints.

## Tax comparison: LMNP vs unfurnished rental

Short-term furnished rental qualifies for LMNP status
            (non-professional furnished lessor), offering either a 50% flat-rate
            deduction (Micro-BIC) or full cost deduction plus property
            depreciation over 20–30 years under the real income regime —
            potentially reducing taxable income to zero for many years.

## Practical examples in Hauts-de-France

A central Lille one-bedroom generating €8,400/year long-term can
            earn €17,472/year net of Welqo's commission via Airbnb — a **+109% gain**. An Arras studio shows a **+143% gain** on comparable numbers.

## Our recommendation

Short-term rental is the right choice if your property is in a
            tourist or business area, you can delegate management to a
            professional, and you are under the real LMNP regime. Welqo can
            simulate your potential short-term revenues before any commitment —
            if the numbers don't stack up, we'll tell you honestly.

